  "statistical_explanation": {
    "root_cause_of_discrepancy": "In Stage 2b, the preliminary bootstrap treated the pooled 11,778 evaluation instances as i.i.d. samples, dividing the sample standard error by sqrt(11,778) \u2248 108.5. This pseudoreplication severely underestimated variance by ignoring cluster-level covariance (samples in the same cluster share vocabulary and semantic frame). In contrast, the fold-level paired t-test (N=15, df=14) captured fold variance but had limited statistical power, yielding p=0.12-0.21. When bootstrapping rigorously over the 209 independent clusters, the true cluster-level confidence interval is correctly estimated."
  }
